From 4dd0d350f466467cd38e0965be071a5d2f401186 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 03:35:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/ppc: add AltiVec HEVC horizontal-only motion
 compensation, uni/bi/uni_w

The inter template already had the pixel-output combines for the vertical
and horizontal-vertical fractions (put_hevc_{qpel,epel}_{uni,bi,uni_w}_{v,hv});
the horizontal-only fractions were still on C. They run on every prediction
unit whose motion vector has a horizontal sub-pel component but no vertical
one, a meaningful minority of inter MC. This adds the six missing kernels:

  ff_hevc_put_qpel_uni_h / _bi_h / _uni_w_h   (8-tap luma)
  ff_hevc_put_epel_uni_h / _bi_h / _uni_w_h   (4-tap chroma)

Each is its vertical sibling with the vertical tap loads replaced by the
horizontal window the first pass of every hv variant already uses
(mc_luma_h16 / mc_chroma_h16): A = mc_load8(src + x - 3), B = mc_load8(src +
x + 5) for luma, x - 1 / x + 7 for chroma, filtered by MC_H8 / MC_H4. The
combine that follows -- the >> (BIT_DEPTH - 8), the uni offset/shift, the bi
src2 add, the uni_w weight, the clip, and the byte-precise mc_store8 -- is
byte-for-byte the vertical sibling's, because the C reference combine is
identical in both directions and differs only in the filter stride. Same
taps, same intermediate widths, same rounding: bit-exact with C.

Registered at width >= 8 on both CPUs alongside the existing v/hv filter
slots in MC_SET; widths 4 and 6, and 12-bit, stay on C as before.

Validated (qemu-ppc-static -cpu 7400, incremental -j1 build, warning-free):
checkasm --test=hevc_pel seeds 13/271828/8675309/42/1/777/5/99/31337/7777
"all 384 tests passed", the six new names dispatching to AltiVec at widths
8/12/16/24/32/48/64 and depths 8 and 10 (84 new entries); full suite
1079/1079 (995 + 84). G5-shape (-D_ARCH_PWR4) compiles clean. Real-G4/G5
--bench pending.

